<http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/articles-metadata.owl> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                                             dc:description """This file includes TARA Clinical Trials Knowledgebase - a structured metadata knowledgebase for acupuncture clinical trial studies developed as part of the TARA Acupoints Research project, encompassing randomized controlled trials, meta-analyses, and systematic reviews of clinical trials. The knowledgebase is derived from metadata extracted from full-text journal publications and is intended to support systematic retrieval, comparison, and quality assessment of acupuncture research studies. 

It includes following classes with a rich set of metadata annotation properties:
- Acupuncture Research Study: the physical execution of an acupuncture clinical trial, from participant recruitment and baseline grouping through administration of real or sham acupuncture procedures to final endpoint evaluation
- Acupuncture Study Publication: the documentary artifact (e.g., journal articles) that reports on an acupuncture trial study
- Acupuncture Study OCSI Appraisal: the structured quality appraisal of acupuncture trial reporting, based on the Oregon CONSORT STRICTA Instrument (OCSI)

Metadata for each publication instance is captured through a standard set of annotation properties organized into three categories:
- Bibliographic Metadata: authorship, source, and publication identifiers
- Study Metadata: intervention design, participant characteristics, sample size, outcome measures, and study outcomes
- OCSI Score Appraisal Metadata: compliance with OCSI criteria for evaluating the completeness and quality of acupuncture trial reporting"""@en ;
                                                                             rdfs:comment """This file includes a set of standard annotation properties that serves as a data dictionary to capture the extracted metadata from acupuncure studies curated for the TARA Project.

Created by: Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X"""@en .

