###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasOutcomesMeasureX2Score
tara-kb:hasOutcomesMeasureX2Score rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> """Standardized Scoring Rubric (0–3 Scale):
- 3 (Excellent): All stated outcome measures (Primary only, OR Primary + Secondary) are clearly defined and explicitly paired with a valid statistical test.
- 2 (Good): Primary outcome measure is clear and mapped, but secondary outcome measures (if present) have ambiguous statistical mapping.
- 1 (Poor): Outcome measures are vague, or statistical methods are listed generally without showing which test applies to which outcome.
- 0 (Non-compliant): Primary outcome measures are not defined, or no statistical testing methods are provided."""@en ,
                                                                               "e.g., a score of 2 when every declared primary outcome is accompanied by a corresponding statistical test, or 0 when outcomes and statistical tests do not align."@en ;
                                  dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                  dcterms:description "A quality metric within Category D: Evaluative Results & Global Metrics that assesses whether a study's primary (and, if applicable, secondary) outcome measures are explicitly defined and directly paired with appropriate, transparent statistical testing methods."@en ;
                                  tara:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasOutcomesMeasureX2Score" ;
                                  rdfs:label "Outcomes Measure X2 Score" ;
                                  skos:prefLabel "Outcomes_Measure_X2_Score" ;
                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasEvaluativeResultsAndGlobalMetrics ;
                                  rdfs:range tara:TARA_5972061 ;
                                  rdfs:domain tara:TARA_2825659 .


