###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasResultsOutcomesScore
tara-kb:hasResultsOutcomesScore rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                                <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> """Standardized Scoring Rubric (0–3 Scale) 
Following the standardized OCSI Likert-like scoring structure, the reporting of results should be scored based on the level of statistical disclosure and data transparency:
- 3 (Full Compliance): The study provides exact data for all predefined outcomes (whether evaluating a single primary outcome or primary + secondary outcomes). This includes specific numbers/estimates, precision metrics (e.g., 95% Confidence Intervals), and exact p-values for each finding.
- 2 (Substantial Compliance): Results are provided for all main outcomes, but exact statistical precision reporting is slightly flawed (e.g., reporting a generic \"p < 0.05\" or omitting confidence intervals for a minor secondary outcome).
- 1 (Partial Compliance): The study omits data for a major outcome, or results are reported selectively/vaguely (e.g., stating in text that \"group differences were not significant\" without actually providing the underlying data table or values).
- 0 (Non-compliance): No empirical results or raw data are presented for the stated primary outcomes, or data reporting is missing entirely."""@en ,
                                                                             "e.g., a score of 2 when reported results directly correspond to the pre-registered outcome measures, or 0 when a mismatch or omission exists."@en ;
                                dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                                dcterms:description "A quality metric within Category D: Evaluative Results & Global Metrics that assesses the completeness, transparency, and accuracy of the reported results for each predefined primary and secondary outcome measure, evaluating whether the text explicitly provides estimated effect sizes, confidence intervals, and precise statistical significance values (e.g., p-values) for each endpoint."@en ;
                                tara:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasResultsOutcomesScore" ;
                                rdfs:comment """To maintain data integrity and prevent construct contamination within the metadata schema, ensure that the data extraction models treat the following two properties separately:
1. hasOutcomesMeasureX2Score (Methodology/Design Check): Focuses on the definition and planned pairing of tests. (e.g., Did they tell us in the Methods section how they planned to calculate the math?)
2. hasResultsOutcomesScore (Reporting/Transparency Check): Focuses on the execution and transparency of the actual data. (e.g., Did they actually show us the exact numbers, tables, effect sizes, and p-values in the Results section?)"""@en ;
                                rdfs:label "Results Outcomes Score" ;
                                skos:prefLabel "Results_Outcomes_Score" ;
                                rdfs:subPropertyOf tara-kb:hasEvaluativeResultsAndGlobalMetrics ;
                                rdfs:range tara:TARA_5972061 ;
                                rdfs:domain tara:TARA_2825659 .


###  http://www.acupunctureresearch.org/tara/ontology/kb/hasSampleSizeDetails
tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "e.g., \"n=84 (42 in intervention, 42 in control)\"."@en ;
                             dcterms:creator "Fahim Imam - https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4752-543X" ;
                             dcterms:description "For the final number of participants who completed the study and were analyzed."@en ;
                             tara:hasCompactURI "tara-kb:hasSampleSizeDetails" ;
                             rdfs:comment "For the final number of participants who completed the study and were analyzed (e.g., \"n=84 (42 in intervention, 42 in control)\")." ;
                             rdfs:label "Sample Size Details" ;
                             skos:prefLabel "Sample_Size_Details" ;
                             rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description ,
                                                tara-kb:hasStudyDesignMetadata ;
                             rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                             rdfs:domain tara:TARA_6701896 .


